Refer to the DeepStream SDK documentation for a description of the "nvinferserver"
plugin and "nvdsinferserver" API.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Pre-requisites:
- GStreamer-1.0 Development package
- GStreamer-1.0 Base Plugins Development package
- CUDA Runtime 13.2

Install gstreamer developement packages using:
   sudo apt-get install libgstreamer-plugins-base1.0-dev libgstreamer1.0-dev \
        libprotobuf-dev protobuf-compiler

Other dependencies:
- Triton client SDK v2.67.0 (nv26.03) for X86
- Triton client SDK v2.68.0 (nv26.04) for aarch64
- Google Protobuf compiler v3.21.12

Install other dependencies (Needs sudo or root privilege):
A. For X86 Device -
1. Triton client SDK into "/opt/tritonclient":
mkdir -p /opt/tritonclient/
rm -rf /opt/tritonclient/lib /opt/tritonclient/include
wget -q -P /tmp https://github.com/triton-inference-server/server/releases/download/v2.67.0/tritonserver-sdk-2.67.0+nv26.03-cu132-cp312-manylinux_2_28-x86_64.zip
unzip -q -o /tmp/tritonserver-sdk-2.67.0+nv26.03-cu132-cp312-manylinux_2_28-x86_64.zip -d /tmp/tritonclient-sdk
mv /tmp/tritonclient-sdk/tritonserver_sdk/install/lib64   /opt/tritonclient/lib
mv /tmp/tritonclient-sdk/tritonserver_sdk/install/include /opt/tritonclient/include
rm -rf /tmp/tritonclient-sdk /tmp/tritonserver-sdk-2.67.0+nv26.03-cu132-cp312-manylinux_2_28-x86_64.zip

2. Protobuf compiler v3.21.12 into "/opt/proto":
mkdir /opt/proto
PB_REL="https://github.com/protocolbuffers/protobuf/releases"
curl -LO $PB_REL/download/v21.12/protoc-21.12-linux-x86_64.zip
unzip protoc-21.12-linux-x86_64.zip -d /opt/proto

B. For Jetson Device -
1. Triton client SDK into "/opt/tritonclient" (the exact asset name/version
   may change between Triton releases — check
   https://github.com/triton-inference-server/server/releases for the latest
   aarch64 SDK zip). Example commands :
mkdir -p /opt/tritonclient/
rm -rf /opt/tritonclient/lib /opt/tritonclient/include
wget -q -P /tmp https://github.com/triton-inference-server/server/releases/download/v2.68.0/tritonserver_sdk-2.68.0+nv26.04-49346681-cu132-cp312-manylinux_2_28-aarch64.zip
unzip -q -o /tmp/tritonserver_sdk-2.68.0+nv26.04-49346681-cu132-cp312-manylinux_2_28-aarch64.zip -d /tmp/tritonclient-sdk
mv /tmp/tritonclient-sdk/tritonserver_sdk/install/lib64   /opt/tritonclient/lib
mv /tmp/tritonclient-sdk/tritonserver_sdk/install/include /opt/tritonclient/include
rm -rf /tmp/tritonclient-sdk /tmp/tritonserver_sdk-2.68.0+nv26.04-49346681-cu132-cp312-manylinux_2_28-aarch64.zip

2. Protobuf compiler v3.21.12 into "/opt/proto":
mkdir /opt/proto
PB_REL="https://github.com/protocolbuffers/protobuf/releases"
curl -LO $PB_REL/download/v21.12/protoc-21.12-linux-aarch_64.zip
unzip protoc-21.12-linux-aarch_64.zip -d /opt/proto
chmod -R +rx /opt/proto/

Please ensure that the above dependencies are installed and update corresponding
paths in the Makefile if required.
Current set paths are as follows:
TRITON_GRPC_CLIENT ?= /opt/tritonclient
PROTOBUF_BIN_DIR ?= /opt/proto/bin

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Compiling and installing the plugin:
Export or set in Makefile the appropriate CUDA_VER
Run make and sudo make install

NOTE:
1. To compile the sources, run make with "sudo" or root permission.
2. Update PATH variable with newly installed protoc by running below command,
   export PATH=/opt/proto/bin/:$PATH
3. Clean and build sources which are compiled with old protoc version.
